<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20994" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hortŭlānus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		hortulus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			garden</i>, <i>garden</i>- (postclass.
			for hortensis). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maritimusque secessus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Poen. 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">porcellus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>stuffed with garden-herbs</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Apic. 8, 7, § 384</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hortulanus</span></b> , i, m., <i>a gardener</i>, <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7,
				3 <i>med.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">App.
				M. 4, p. 143</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9</span></i>, p. 235 sq.;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4200</span></i>.</div>
